this mission to northeast asia ended  as it had begun with the u.s directly  accusing  china of aggressive behavior in the  region but the u.s and south korea  also confirmed beijing's importance in  the denuclearization of north korea  but china has a real interest in helping  to deal with this it also has an  obligation  under the u.n security council  resolutions the u.s had tried to open a  dialogue with north korea  ahead of this trip but without success  north korea has officially confirmed it  had received those requests  but didn't respond its first vice  foreign minister chai son he  saying there can be no dialogue until  the u.s  stops what she called its hostile  behavior  making it clear pyongyang is waiting to  see  what the new policy of the biden  administration towards it  will look like this mission is intended  to help formulate that strategy  it's also aimed at restoring and  repairing relations between the us  and its traditional allies in northeast  asia  as the u.s has repeatedly said the  trilateral security cooperation between  seoul tokyo and washington is crucial  considering the international situation  and newly emerging security threats  relations often severely strained during  the previous administration of donald  trump  that advantage for the united states has  been greatly  uh ruined during the four years of trump  administration  so it is important for the biden  administration to  restore the strategic asset that united  states has  and china does not one of the last acts  on this visit  a cost-sharing agreement for the basing  of u.s troops in south korea  disputed for years by the trump  administration  its final signing seen here as evidence  of an alliance restored rob mcbride al  jazeera seoul
 

